# the ELF encoding of trait axes
#
# one row per encoding ELF has of a trait axis, keyed by the axis row of the
# trait catalog and the kind of its field, giving where its value lives and
# the constant that encodes each value. a value lives in bits of e_flags, in
# bits of a GNU property whose data is one word, as the and and or feature
# properties are, or in an attribute of a subsection of the build attributes
# section. an axis may have several encodings, as AArch64 states branch
# protection both in a GNU property and in a build attribute. the writer
# encodes an object's traits through every row of each axis, and the reader
# decodes each row, refusing a file whose encodings of one axis state
# different values, so a bit or attribute a row maps is the row's alone and
# is never also kept raw.

